<title>MEXICO: MEXICO'S 28-DAY CETES RATE 18.71 PCT IN AUCTION.</title>
<headline>MEXICO'S 28-DAY CETES RATE 18.71 PCT IN AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction on Tuesday as demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent) Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	18.71	    + 36	    18.48     18.95</p>
<p>91-Day	19.63	    + 45	    19.35     19.73</p>
<p>182-Day     20.77	    + 38	    20.65     20.85</p>
<p>350-Day     20.84				20.75     20.93</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 20.52 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.26 bln pesos    2.82</p>
<p>91-Day	1.0 bln pesos   2.37 bln pesos    2.37</p>
<p>182-Day     1.0 bln pesos   2.75 bln pesos    2.75</p>
<p>350-Day     800 million pesos   3.11 bln pesos    3.89</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 2.91 on demand of 10.49 billion pesos compared to 3.70 the week before on demand of 11.11 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   24 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   10 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   8 basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			   9 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
